Authentication & Authorization

Authentication - who are you? verify user using username and password

Authorization - what are you allowed to do? which resources a user can access

JWT - JSON web token send information client to server
Login -> call api -> to view

Header.Payload.Signature

cvbnmgfbnjsd7678.dcvbnmkuyd.edfghtr456yhg

Header -> information about the token
{
"typ" : "JWT",
"alg":"HS256"
}

payload -> information such as user identity and expity time
{
    "email":
    "role":Student
    "exp":44125426
}

Signature -> HS256 algo

helps server to detect whether the token has been modified

"eyJhbGciOiJFUzI1NiIsvtpZCI6Ijc5YmU5YjI5LWVkZGUtNDhhZi1hZmM2LTJiYzhlZDI5ZDVkMiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..emjNtG6coqT-0W9_gR1wBbsn96Iy1WZ894wWgnluzGt8hlSpuFvg1dhsya00f8FchA8_fowZL-6z9jrNgryRAA"

    step 1 : Login  (username and password)
    step 2 : verify credentials - server checks whether they are correct
    STep 3 : Generate JWT server - return an access token
    step 4 : Access protected api - client sends the token with each request
    step 5 : Verify token and permissions - server accepts or rejects the request


